  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Monteroni The Monteroni necropolis preserved evidence of tumulus-type tombs with rich funerary assemblages dating to the third century B.C. The earliest use of the necropolis likely belongs to the seventh century B.C.</p>",
